      "message": "The original code seems rather convoluted and complex. Your change here doesn\u0027t make it worse, but they don\u0027t really simplify it either. I feel we can make it much much simpler, and wanted your thoughts on whether my proposal is feasible.\n\nWhy can\u0027t we simply have:\n* Every target contains a std::optional\u003cTargetInfo\u003e\n* It can be safely initialized in Builder::OnDefined (the constructor only cares that dependencies have been added)\n\nThen we don\u0027t need to synchronize anything or worry about these use-after-free things. We know that the lifetime perfectly matches.\n\n```\nResolvedTargetData::TargetInfo* ResolvedTargetData::GetTargetInfo(\n    const Target* target) const {\n  return \u0026target-\u003einfo();\n}\n```",
